    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the Texas primary runoff, an election candidate secured a decisive victory with strong voter support, winning about 64% of the vote to end a long-serving senator's bid. This outcome was aided by a late endorsement from the sitting president, a political leader whose timely support helped shape the result. The affected incumbent, a senator who had substantially outraised his rival, now faces an unprecedented loss, becoming the first sitting Republican senator from Texas to lose renomination since 1970. The election winner will now move to the general election, entering a new contest that could reshape control of the U.S. Senate.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
