    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Supported by a presidential endorsement, the candidate endorsed by the president overcame a significant financial disadvantage to achieve victory in the runoff. Despite the long-serving senator whose bid was ended outraising and outspending him, the election winner claimed a nomination that ousts an incumbent. This historical first in Texas politics marks the end of a decades-long streak of renominations for the veteran senator. Now, the politician is set to compete in a high-stakes race affecting Senate control, moving to the general election against a Democratic state representative in November.",
